# VAPT Guardrails — ASP.NET Core

Apply when editing controllers, auth, or upload code. **Always-on:** F4, F8, F9, F10. **Regression:** F1, F3. An applicable failure is Critical.

## F1 — Session end

Logout clears the auth cookie and the server session. A denylist or session store fails closed.

## F3 — Uploads

Validate size, content type, and structure on the server. Store a generated name. Cap decompression. Require authorization. Production scans for malware.

## F4 — Authorization

`[Authorize]` on every admin or mutation action. Anonymous access is `[AllowAnonymous]` and local-dev only. Policy failures deny. A missing attribute is not public.

## F8 — Object access

A same-role caller cannot read or write another owner's `{id}`. The owning service checks it. Write DTOs reject unknown properties.

## F9 — Authentication

Authentication middleware runs before handlers. JWT checks `iss`, `aud`, `exp`, and `nbf`. Fail closed.

## F10 — Audit

Audit auth, denial, admin mutation, and upload outcome. Do not log the token.

## F5 — Exposed API calls (LOW)

A client bundle must not call an admin route the user cannot use. Hiding a button is not authorization. Record the finding. It blocks only when the diff makes the call exploitable.

## F6 — Multiple sessions (LOW)

Document single-session or multi-session. When the policy is single-session, a new login invalidates the previous token for that user.
